4.2 Bodhi Navigator --- Your Study and Practice GPS
Core features:
The map shows the path of awakening with 10 major stations, 42 sub-stations, and over 700 lessons
A red marker shows your current position (current lesson)
A boat icon represents your study identity (Scholarly, Practitioner, Victorious, Sagacious)
Five Areas of Mindful Engagement: self-study, group study, daily practice, daily life, serving the community
When you open Bodhi Navigator each day, you will see:
1. What to study today
2. What daily practice to do today
3. Today's mental reminder
4.3 MetaNote --- From Black to White Transformation
The personality code chain:
Cultural heritage → Ways of thinking → Views → Behaviors → Habits → Character → Personality
Black and White Cards:
Black card: Record a current negative mental state (anger, jealousy, anxiety), analyze its source, find the antidote
White card: Record a current moment of mindfulness and wholesome mind (gratitude, rejoicing, mindfulness), reinforce through repetition
Key insight: Life can be designed. Through MetaNote, you can take inventory of your mind, choose what to cultivate, and transform it.
