6.3 Eight Things for Students (Collective Joy Course Foundation)
1. Lay the attitude foundation: honest, earnest, committed, self-motivated
2. Self-study habit: Set a daily self-study time
3. Group study attitude: Participate actively, rejoice and praise
4. Consistency in daily practice: Maintain daily practice
5. Make good use of tools: Bodhi Navigator, MetaNote, etc.
6. Mindfulness meditation: Practice beginner-level mindfulness
7. Loving-kindness meditation: Practice the beginner-level *Metta Chanting*
8. Altruistic meditation: Practice gratitude, rejoicing, understanding, sympathy, acceptance
6.4 Growth Is Not "Leveling Up"
Key insight: Growth is not about obtaining a title --- it is about becoming a better version of yourself. Identities are signposts, not destinations. Every step of study and practice helps you move away from suffering toward happiness, and grow in wisdom and compassion.
