How to Make the Best Use of These Two Handbooks
The *Mindful Peace Academy Student Handbook* is a comprehensive study and practice manual. It covers in detail the origins of Mindful Peace Academy, curriculum structure, growth paths, methods of study and practice, conventions and guidelines, and more. It is your "encyclopedia" on the path of study and practice --- well worth reading again and again and consulting whenever needed.
![](media/image9.png){width="3.5433048993875764in" height="0.36909667541557306in"}50
And this *Mindful Peace Academy: Introductory Study Guide* in your hands right now is a "quick-start map." It extracts the most essential and commonly used parts of the Student Handbook, using simpler language closer to new students, to help you quickly understand:
- Why should I study? (Study and practice orientation)
- How should I study? (Attitudes, methods, tools)
- What do I need to pay attention to? (Conventions, help channels)
Here's how we suggest you use them:
1. Read the *Mindful Peace Academy: Introductory Study Guide* first --- in the shortest time, get an overall picture of study and practice, know where to start and roughly how each step unfolds.
2. Then read the *Mindful Peace Academy Student Handbook* --- once you have the basic concepts, dive into the handbook's detailed content. You'll find it easier to understand and remember.
3. When you encounter questions, come back and consult them anytime --- both handbooks can serve as daily references. The *Introductory Study Guide* helps you quickly find direction; the *Student Handbook* gives you complete answers.
We believe that when you light the first lamp through the *Introductory Study Guide*, then step into the broader world of the *Student Handbook*, you will enter the role of a practitioner more quickly and walk the path of awakening more steadily.
Let everyone become the master of their own study and practice --- may these two handbooks be your most faithful companions on the journey.
